+
+# 2026-11-01
+
+## Done
+
+- Added `GET /api/admin/users/recently-created`, admin only, returning the logins of users whose `createdDate` is within the last 7 days, most recent first.
+- Query in `UserRepository.findLoginsCreatedSince`, window logic in `UserService.getRecentlyCreatedUserLogins`, endpoint in `UserResource`.
+- Added Liquibase changelog `20261101120000_added_index_jhi_user_created_date` (index on `jhi_user.created_date`), registered in `master.xml`, because the query filters on that column.
+- Build not run and no tests added, as requested.
+- Review fix: the 7-day window now uses an injected `java.time.Clock` (new `config/ClockConfiguration` bean, passed into `UserService`) instead of `Instant.now()`. The endpoint's `@PreAuthorize` already uses `AuthoritiesConstants.ADMIN`.
+
+## Next
+
+- Run `./mvnw verify` and add an integration test for the endpoint.
+- Decide whether the frontend needs a view for this list.
+- `GET /api/admin/users/{login}` now shadows any user whose login is exactly `recently-created`.
+- Pre-existing `Instant.now()` calls in `UserService` (password reset checks, activation cleanup scheduler) do not use the clock. Out of scope here; migrate them to the injected `Clock` separately.
